      "controlled_text": [
        {
          "id": "beacon_1",
          "text": "At noon, the harbor beacon can draw current from the grid or from a charged backup battery. Either source alone provides current; with neither source there is no current. The selector always uses an available source and needs no operator action. The lamp illuminates exactly when current is available and its opaque safety shutter is open. A closed shutter prevents illumination even with current. These rules hold throughout the noon inspection; no other faults or inputs are in scope.",
          "episode": "controlled time indices",
          "source_id": "beacon",
          "source_type": "authored controlled narrative",
          "url": "controlled://v3/beacon_1",
          "dependence_cluster": "beacon",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 486,
          "first_line": 1,
          "last_line": 1,
          "scene": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "beacon_2",
          "text": "During the inspection the grid and the charged backup battery were both available, the shutter was open, current reached the lamp, and the beacon was illuminated. A clerk rang the lunch bell one minute later. The bell is electrically separate and does not operate the beacon.",
          "episode": "controlled time indices",
          "source_id": "beacon",
