      "controlled_text": [
        {
          "id": "ferry_1",
          "text": "At ten, Iona stood at the ferry with a stamped permit in her hand and a boat ready at the landing. She showed the permit to the watchman. He inspected it, lifted the chain across the landing, and she carried the parcel aboard. At eleven the ferry crossed with the parcel. The account does not say whether a permit is indispensable, whether exceptions are allowed, or what happens when a boat is not ready. A causal influence of permission on departure is suggested by the exchange, but a universal policy is not recorded.",
          "episode": "controlled time indices",
          "source_id": "ferry",
          "source_type": "authored controlled narrative",
          "url": "controlled://v3/ferry_1",
          "dependence_cluster": "ferry",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 521,
          "first_line": 1,
          "last_line": 1,
          "scene": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "ferry_2",
          "text": "The controlled delivery system has this rule: a parcel crossing on the ferry before noon is always recorded as delivered at the far-bank station, and a parcel that does not cross before noon is not recorded there. No other route or recording failure is possible in this system. Today the parcel was recorded as delivered. At twelve Iona announced that she believed the permit had guaranteed success. Her later announcement is a belief about the completed trip, not a prior instruction to the ferry.",
          "episode": "controlled time indices",
          "source_id": "ferry",
          "source_type": "authored controlled narrative",
          "url": "controlled://v3/ferry_2",
          "dependence_cluster": "ferry",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 498,
          "first_line": 1,
          "last_line": 1,
          "scene": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "ferry_3",
          "text": "For this diagnostic, the only varying inputs to whether the parcel crosses are permit possession and boat readiness at ten. The omitted departure rule is some fixed deterministic Boolean function of these two inputs. Its factual output with both inputs present is crossing. The missing three configurations are not disclosed; investigators must not infer them from chronology or Iona's claim. Permission and physical departure are different events even if an analyst chooses to model their combined consequence.",
          "episode": "controlled time indices",
          "source_id": "ferry",
          "source_type": "authored controlled narrative",
          "url": "controlled://v3/ferry_3",
          "dependence_cluster": "ferry",
          "start": 0,
